{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FigureEightBranchingRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FigureEightBranchingRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.row_or_col_degenerate_of_skewSYTCount_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.row_or_col_degenerate_of_skewSYTCount_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.lean#L94-L101","doc":"b_λ = 0 iff λ does not contain [2,1] as a sub-diagram,\nwhich holds iff λ is a single row or single column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_b_zero_iff_row_or_col_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_b_zero_iff_row_or_col_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**External axiom (manuscript §5.11): b_λ = 0 iff λ is single\nrow or single column** (no [2,1] sub-diagram fits otherwise). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_b_nonpositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_b_nonpositive","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.lean#L77-L82","doc":"The q-correction coefficient b_λ = -f^{λ/[2,1]} is always ≤ 0,\nsince skewSYTCount returns a natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_branching_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.figure_eight_branching_rule","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.lean#L34-L75","doc":"The figure-eight character in irrep λ of H_k(q) decomposes\nvia the branching rule H_k(q) ↓ H_3(q).\n\nProof: by induction on k.\nBase (k=3): f^{μ/μ} = 1, f^{μ/ν} = 0 for ν ≠ μ.\nStep (k→k+1): Pieri rule + IH reassembles skew SYT counts.\n\n**But this declaration asserts nothing, and is kept only so the\nlabel resolves.**\n\nBoth its hypothesis and its conclusion are syntactic tautologies:\n`h_chi : chi_actual = chi_actual` is discharged by `rfl` and so\nconstrains no caller, and the conclusion is `E = E` for one\nexpression `E`.  The comment in the proof body says as much --\n*\"The identity is trivially reflexive; the content is in the\nINTERPRETATION\"* -- and that is exactly the problem: the\ninterpretation is not in the type, so nothing here is checked.\n\nIt escapes every axiom gate, because it is a `theorem`: there is no\n`axiom` to print, no axiom status to move, and the corpus vacuity\naudit keys on a `: True` conclusion, which `E = E` is not.\n\nA statement with content needs `χ(4₁, λ)` as a *defined* quantity\nand the branching identity as an equation between two *different*\nexpressions.  `skewSYTCount` is `opaque … := fun _ _ => 0`, so that\nis not available here, and it is deliberately not guessed at. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:figure-eight-branching-rule","label":"prop:figure-eight-branching-rule","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.skewSYTCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.skewSYTCount","kind":"opaque","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/figure-eight-branching-rule.lean#L22-L32","doc":"Number of standard Young tableaux of skew shape outer/inner.\n\n**Axiomatised (§3b-cond)**: equivalently, number of saturated\nchains from inner to outer in Young's lattice.  Pending the\nMathlib StandardYoungTableau enumeration. ","signatureChunk":0}]}